    {
      "topic": "consequence",
      "statement": "The after HTML callbacks render a spoiler span with opening <x-spoiler> and closing </x-spoiler> tags. Their image-nesting guards suppress nested tags inside image labels, so an ordinary paragraph provides a route without that guard.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "unit_id": "u-7bb4879720e3cda5d58e",
          "start_line": 456,
          "end_line": 469,
          "role": "primary",
